; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Op Art Waves
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     op art, sine waves, FILLED, stripes, illusion
; SUMMARY:  Paints black and white stripes that bulge and ripple, an optical illusion in the style of Bridget Riley.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Thirty stripes cross the screen. Each stripe's edges follow a
;   sine wave, and the waves get taller near the middle of the
;   screen and flatter at the edges. Every other stripe is painted
;   black. Stare at it and the picture seems to move.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :waves or :height near the bottom.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a function of x that gives the edge of a stripe
;   * FILLED shapes whose outline comes from a formula
;   * walking along one edge and back along the other
;   * stripes that touch but never overlap
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set :height to 0. The illusion vanishes.
;   * Use two colors that are close, like navy and teal.
;   * Make the stripes vertical by swapping x and y in EDGE.Y.
; ============================================================

; EDGE.Y gives the height of the line between stripes number :k at
; position :x. Stripes are 20 apart, and the wave is tallest at
; x = 0 and dies away toward both sides.
to edge.y :k :x
  localmake "swell :height * (1 - (:x / 400) * (:x / 400))
  output :k * 20 - 300 + :swell * sin (:x * :waves + :k * 12)
end

; STRIPE paints the strip between edge :k and edge :k + 1.
to stripe :k :color
  penup setxy -400 edge.y :k -400
  filled :color [
    ; along the lower edge, left to right...
    for [x -400 400 10] [setxy :x edge.y :k :x]
    ; ...and back along the upper edge, right to left.
    for [x 400 -400 -10] [setxy :x edge.y :k + 1 :x]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7
make "waves 1.4
make "height 40
; Only the black stripes need painting; white is the background.
; Edges -1 to 31 cover the whole screen even where the waves dip.
for [k -1 31 2] [stripe :k [10 10 10]]
